      'Turn-flow example: On turn, play one hand card to match month cards in the center layout and capture according to matching rules, then reveal the top stock card and resolve captures again. Special capture events and bonus transfers apply when specific board states occur. When your captures reach the minimum score, you may stop to end the hand and collect, or choose go to continue and increase potential payout while risking a loss to an opponent.',
      'Scoring example: Scores are built from captured card categories and named combinations; payout multipliers increase after each successful go in many tables. Hand winner is the first player to stop after reaching threshold, or an opponent who overtakes and ends the hand under agreed rules..',
